e-run by me rather than trusted from the implementer's notes.\n\nWhy I existed at all: the prior reviewer run finished its code reading but ended its turn while its test runs were still in the background, which kills them in a spawned session — so no verdict got recorded. I re-verified everything first-person and waited on the long suite in-turn this time.\n\nWhat I verified:\n\n- **Behavior and validation** — `add` enforces exactly-one-source and validates before touching the config file; `login` validates the scope and loads the config *before* prompting, stores through `gitcred.StoreScoped` (proved by read-back), then selects `token=keyring`; `list` prints sorted lines with a live `present=` probe; `remove` errors on unconfigured scopes and deletes the stored token only for keyring scopes — never the operator's own git-credential, which a dedicated test pins. Invalid-invocation matrices cover add, login, and remove, plus a full round trip against a real isolated `credential.helper=store`.\n- **No token in argv** — no flag on this surface carries a literal secret; `login` reads a hidden `term.ReadPassword` prompt or one stdin line, and the config layer independently rejects a secret pasted into `token`. The one `--token` flag in main.go is the pre-existing audit-publish registry token, untouched.\n- **Help vs spec** — I read curator-spec `core.md` §12.2 directly: the help documents the unbound `CURATOR_BUILD_HTTPS_TOKEN` exposure, the `CURATOR_BUILD_HTTPS_HOST` binding, and operator ownership, exactly as the spec's MUSTs require; ordering is test-pinned.\n- **Gates** — `go build`, `go vet`, `gofmt`, `golangci-lint` (0 issues), `internal/config` + `internal/gitcred` tests, and the full `go test ./cmd/curator/... -timeout 30m` all green (518.6s, log in `.temp/TASK-260825-2gyhq8/`).\n\nThree minor non-blocking observations are recorded in the verdict artifact (`TASK-260825-2gyhq8_review-verdict.md` on the board): a post-prompt username-length validation edge in `login` that can orphan a namespaced keyring entry in an absurd case, username charset rejection happening only at broker time, and one test probing the real credential helper read-only.\n\nOne flag for the orchestrator, outside this task's scope: LOGBOOK.md entry 0130 (from the already-accepted TASK-260825-168m7o) names the external reference project by absolute path, which the epic policy forbids in document artifacts — worth scrubbing before the scope is committed. Per the reviewer constraint I supplied no `commit_ack`; the commit-owning mover owns committing this uncommitted shared-tree scope.","ttft_ms":3256,"ttft_stream_ms":1683,"time_to_request_ms":31,"type":"result","duration_ms":672286,"uuid":"c320dc1a-1e29-4d74-a6d2-b21f9064b4a8"}
